From 5c24c9fbb7d82272c2459820769ab44615c9cde5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 21:03:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] VideoPlayerVideo: one eye of a full frame of 3D given the
 size of the whole frame

The display size of a picture of two views is taken for the size of one
eye (CBaseRenderer::ManageRenderArea() takes its aspect for the eye's).
That holds for a half frame of side by side or top and bottom, for a
container that gives the size of one eye, and for the views that Hades
puts side by side itself (MultiviewChoice.h halves the sample aspect).
A full frame given the size of the whole frame (a 3840x1080 side by side
at a sample aspect of 1, a .3D.FSBS. file named as such) made each eye
twice as wide as it is, and a full top and bottom one half as wide.

An eye wider than 2.6:1 (side by side) or narrower than 1.3:1 (top and
bottom) is now taken for such a frame, and its display size is halved
in the direction of the two views; the 3D films released are between
these at any resolution (2.39:1 to 1.43:1). The rule is in
StereoEyeSize.h, and kodi.log says once a stream when it acts. Hades'
own packed views (MVC, MV-HEVC) are not changed: their eye is 1.78:1.

From Portisch's change for CoreELEC (CoreELEC/xbmc commit 40f14dcdbe,
"VideoPlayerVideo: fix the eye aspect of full packed stereo frames"),
here as a function of its own with the same limits.
